Subject: [PATCH] interface: reconcile live device IPv6 family changes

A live disable_ipv6 change does not tear down a dual-stack interface. Notify
the existing L3 subscribers and reconcile their IPv6 addresses, routes,
neighbors, delegated prefixes and installed policy rules without disturbing
IPv4. Retain desired netifd-owned state for re-enable, but require fresh
protocol publication for external IPv6 snapshots. Alias devices mirror the
underlying effective setting. Publish only active prefix ownership.

